WEBVTT

00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:30.628
And if you can’t start with a subject line
with an action verb,

00:01:30.628 --> 00:01:32.213
you shouldn’t have the meeting.

00:01:32.463 --> 00:01:34.799
“Decide, finalize, create next steps.”

00:01:34.966 --> 00:01:36.717
Those are reasons to call a meeting.

00:01:36.926 --> 00:01:40.263
“Review,” on the other hand,
isn’t an action verb.

00:01:40.263 --> 00:01:42.515
If you're calling a meeting
to review something,

00:01:42.515 --> 00:01:43.766
send it out ahead of time

00:01:43.766 --> 00:01:45.977
and schedule a 15-minute
meeting for questions.

00:01:46.269 --> 00:01:48.396
That should get Joe
to finally read the deck.

00:01:48.688 --> 00:01:50.398
Related to that action verb,

00:01:50.398 --> 00:01:51.983
if you’re going to call a meeting

00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:54.569
you should be able to create
a clear purpose statement.

00:01:54.569 --> 00:01:57.655
“In this meeting we’re going to decide
boom, boom, boom.

00:01:57.655 --> 00:01:58.698
Come prepared.”

00:01:58.906 --> 00:02:00.366
You don’t need a whole agenda;